    {
      "text": "Figure 7. Trajectory analysis and graph abstraction of mouse intestinal epithelium data from Haber et al (2017).",
      "x0": 50.513414,
      "y0": 398.729108,
      "x1": 411.744389,
      "y1": 407.795048
    },
    {
      "text": "(A) Distal and proximal enterocyte differentiation trajectories inferred by Slingshot. The Distal lineage is shown coloured by pseudotime from red to blue. Other cells in the",
      "x0": 50.513414,
      "y0": 411.629256,
      "x1": 544.764769,
      "y1": 418.073047
    },
    {
      "text": "dataset are grey. (B) Slingshot trajectories over clusters in PCA space. Clusters are abbreviated as follows: EP\u2014enterocyte progenitors; Imm. Ent.\u2014immature enterocytes;",
      "x0": 50.513414,
      "y0": 420.870253,
      "x1": 544.752186,
      "y1": 427.314044
    },
    {
      "text": "Mat. Ent.\u2014mature enterocytes; Prox.\u2014proximal; Dist.\u2014distal. (C) Density over pseudotime for the distal enterocyte trajectory from Fig 7A. Colours represent the dominant",
      "x0": 50.513414,
      "y0": 430.11122,
      "x1": 544.725003,
      "y1": 436.555011
    },
    {
      "text": "cluster labels in each pseudotime bin. (D) Abstracted graph representation of the dataset projected onto a UMAP representation. Clusters are shown as coloured nodes.",
      "x0": 50.512712,
      "y0": 439.352187,
      "x1": 541.873415,
      "y1": 445.795978
    },
    {
      "text": "Clusters that appear in other trajectories are labelled for comparison. \u201cTA\u201d denotes transit amplifying cells. (E) Gene expression dynamics over pseudotime in a general",
      "x0": 50.512712,
      "y0": 446.975263,
      "x1": 541.193477,
      "y1": 456.041203
    },
    {
      "text": "enterocyte trajectory using the \u201cGAM\u201d R library.",
      "x0": 50.513414,
      "y0": 456.21626,
      "x1": 191.055009,
      "y1": 465.2822
    },
    {
      "text": "salmonella infection has been shown to increase the proportion of the microbiome literature (Gloor et al, 2017), where compositional",
      "x0": 42.519699,
      "y0": 489.708258,
      "x1": 552.745567,
      "y1": 497.576101
    },
    {
      "text": "enterocytes in the mouse intestinal epithelium (Haber et al, 2017). data analysis has received more attention.",
      "x0": 42.519699,
      "y0": 501.046576,
      "x1": 457.592027,
      "y1": 508.91445
    },
    {
      "text": "Investigating compositional changes in single-cell data requires",
      "x0": 53.631451,
      "y0": 512.389013,
      "x1": 289.149568,
      "y1": 520.252737
    },
    {
      "text": "sufficient cell numbers to robustly assess cell-identity cluster Pitfalls & recommendations:",
      "x0": 42.519699,
      "y0": 523.727346,
      "x1": 408.739927,
      "y1": 532.929155
    },
    {
      "text": "proportions, and sufficient sample numbers to evaluate expected",
      "x0": 42.519699,
      "y0": 535.065649,
      "x1": 289.173544,
      "y1": 542.929373
    },
    {
      "text": "\u2022 Consider that statistical tests over changes in the proportion of a cell-",
      "x0": 311.6409,
      "y0": 537.333679,
      "x1": 538.732626,
      "y1": 554.170629
    },
    {
      "text": "background variation in cell-identity cluster compositions. As appro-",
      "x0": 42.519699,
      "y0": 546.403967,
      "x1": 289.189255,
      "y1": 554.267691
    },
    {
      "text": "identity cluster between samples are dependent on one another.",
      "x0": 319.067688,
      "y0": 552.039667,
      "x1": 520.972905,
      "y1": 558.951082
    },
    {
      "text": "priate datasets have only recently become available, dedicated tools",
      "x0": 42.519699,
      "y0": 557.742285,
      "x1": 289.162794,
      "y1": 565.606009
    },
    {
      "text": "are yet to be developed. In the mouse study mentioned above, cell-",
      "x0": 42.519699,
      "y0": 569.080603,
      "x1": 289.139642,
      "y1": 576.944327
    },
    {
      "text": "identity counts were modelled using a Poisson process, including Trajectory analysis",
      "x0": 42.519699,
      "y0": 580.418921,
      "x1": 374.314639,
      "y1": 588.282644
    },
    {
      "text": "the condition as a covariate, and the total number of cells detected Trajectory inference",
      "x0": 42.519699,
      "y0": 591.757238,
      "x1": 372.539306,
      "y1": 599.620962
    },
    {
      "text": "as an offset. Here, a statistical test can be performed over the regres- Cellular diversity cannot sufficiently be described by a discrete clas-",
      "x0": 42.519699,
      "y0": 603.095556,
      "x1": 552.780653,
      "y1": 611.07485
    },
    {
      "text": "sion coefficient to assess whether a particular cell identity has signif- sification system such as clustering. The biological processes that",
      "x0": 42.519699,
      "y0": 614.433859,
      "x1": 552.772385,
      "y1": 622.413168
    },
    {
      "text": "icantly changed in frequency. However, tests over other cell drive the development of the observed heterogeneity are continuous",
      "x0": 42.519699,
      "y0": 625.772177,
      "x1": 552.736002,
      "y1": 633.751471
    },
    {
      "text": "identities in the same dataset are not independent of each other. If processes (Tanay & Regev, 2017). Thus, in order to capture transi-",
      "x0": 42.519699,
      "y0": 637.110495,
      "x1": 552.793057,
      "y1": 645.089789
    },
    {
      "text": "the proportion of one cell-identity cluster changes, the proportions tions between cell identities, branching differentiation processes, or",
      "x0": 42.519699,
      "y0": 648.448813,
      "x1": 552.786442,
      "y1": 656.428106
    },
    {
      "text": "of all others must have changed as well. Thus, one cannot assess gradual, unsynchronized changes in biological function, we require",
      "x0": 42.519699,
      "y0": 659.78713,
      "x1": 552.810422,
      "y1": 667.766424
    },
    {
      "text": "whether the overall composition has significantly changed using this dynamic models of gene expression. This class of methods is known",
      "x0": 42.519699,
      "y0": 671.125441,
      "x1": 552.755021,
      "y1": 679.104742
    },
    {
      "text": "model. In the absence of dedicated tools, visual comparison of as trajectory inference (TI).",
      "x0": 42.519699,
      "y0": 682.463759,
      "x1": 404.549045,
      "y1": 690.443052
    },
    {
      "text": "compositional data can be informative of changes in compositions Trajectory inference methods interpret single-cell data as a snapshot",
      "x0": 42.519699,
      "y0": 693.802069,
      "x1": 552.783142,
      "y1": 701.781378
    },
    {
      "text": "between samples (Fig 6C). Future developments in this field will of a continuous process. This process is reconstructed by finding paths",
